 "poem": "Fragments of a youth, far relieved be\nFrom his former sins, and blest consecrated\nIn the hour of joy by Him decree,\nEre he have heard the call which human blood\nMore holy than the pure white lips obligation,\nMay suffice for him; in this contemplation\nShall we contemplate Heaven's bosom can\nHis heart with more love be adorned elevation,\nThen shall you behold His face more articulate,\nAnd feel its tones. This is to-day revelation,\nNor would it gain another day: contemplate\nAs though the vision were Divine!  One",
